step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a robust median combination on pool1 to see if a smaller, stable pool improves performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: test a simple best_single strategy using the top performer rf to see if a single model can beat the robust combinations.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"rf"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean over the full pool to see if trimming improves over the plain mean and best_single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the moderately stable pool2 to see if restricting to more stable models improves over full‑pool median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Try a DTW barycenter over the most stable pool (pool3) to see if that improves on best_single rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool3","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a robust median over the most stable pool3 to see if it improves on best_single rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool3"}

Thought: Test a dba over pool1 to see if a smaller stable pool improves over best_single rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the existing meta-weight handle w1 on the stable pool3 to see if focusing weights on the most consistent models improves over best_single rf.

Action: evaluate_strategy
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool3","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean over the more stable pool2 (k=7) to see if a smaller, more stable subset improves over the full pool.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool2","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using handle w2 which was trained on pool3, to see if a different weighting improves over the current best single rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool3","weights":"w2"}

Thought: Test a different best_single model to see if a single model can beat rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ETS"}

Thought: Test a DTW barycenter over the more stable pool2 to see if it improves on best_single rf and other robust combos.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool2","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean over the most stable pool (pool3) to see if trimming improves over the plain mean and best_single rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool3","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a different best_single model (ARIMA) to see if a single model can beat rf.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the full model pool with the pre‑computed handle w1 to see if the meta‑model weighting improves on best_single rf.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a different single model, THETA, to see if it can beat RF.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"THETA"}

